# Colang output rails for Squire (NeMo Guardrails v0.21.0)
#
# The `bot inform answer unknown` override in input.co covers both
# directions (NeMo's PII subflow emits the same utterance on input-side
# and output-side hits). This file is intentionally empty except for a
# placeholder comment so the rails/ directory remains non-empty and any
# future Squire-specific output customisation has a natural home.
#
# When the output-side PII detector fires and the BLOCKED_BY_RAIL line is
# returned to nemo_client.parse_block, the rail_name field is "input"
# (string constant in the refusal message). The Squire response_builder
# emits the block with that rail_name; the rule_name "presidio_pii" is
# what downstream consumers actually key on. If distinguishing input vs
# output attribution becomes important, the fix is to read NeMo's
# /v1/chat/completions `events` array (where source is carried
# structurally), not the content string.
